# Astro emits content-hashed filenames under /_astro/ (JS, fonts, images) — safe to
# cache forever. HTML is intentionally NOT given a rule here: Cloudflare Pages already
# serves it as `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate` by default, so deploys are picked
# up immediately.
#
# Do NOT add a broad `/*` Cache-Control rule. Cloudflare Pages COMBINES the headers of
# every matching rule, so `/*` concatenates onto `/_astro/*` and produces a corrupt
# asset header with two max-age values (max-age=31536000 ... , max-age=0). Keep the
# only Cache-Control rule scoped to the immutable asset path.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
